# The API image is built with the repository root as its context, because a
# pnpm workspace build needs the root manifest, the lockfile and the workspace
# packages the API depends on — not just apps/api.
#
# Everything listed here is excluded from the tarball the daemon receives, so
# it can neither slow the build down nor invalidate a layer. The rule of thumb:
# if it is generated, secret, or only meaningful on a developer's machine, it
# does not belong in the context.

# Generated, and regenerated inside the image anyway. Copying a host build in
# would also mix glibc-linked native artifacts into a musl image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
apps/api/src/generated
coverage
**/coverage
.turbo
**/.turbo

# History and tooling state. .git alone is tens of megabytes and changes on
# every commit, which would bust the context hash for no benefit.
.git
.github
.husky
.claude
.superpowers

# Secrets never belong in a build context: anything here would land in an
# image layer, readable by anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local infrastructure and documentation — not inputs to the runtime image.
docker
docker-compose.yml
docs
scripts
**/*.md

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.log
.vscode
.idea
